From d16adef98a8c5afdd1c3866246bb9e3fe8b837c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Crittenden <rcritten@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Jan 2026 19:11:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Allow requesting a ML-DSA key using a strength

I was discouraged from treating the numeric portion of ML-DSA
algorithms as a "strength" per-se but it seems like other
crypto products are doing it so I'm adding it for consistentcy.

Interally certmonger will use the full name if a key type of
ML-DSA is requested. The default will be ML-DSA-65.

While implementing this I discovered there is a public function
for identifying the ML key type in NSS given a private key blob
so I switched that out in this as well.
